/-!
# A genus-two Belyi record and its elliptic primitivization

This file certifies two related rows of the LMFDB tables of Belyi maps.

The passport `3T1-3_3_3` is the cyclic cover of degree three, totally ramified over `0`, `1` and
`∞`: its stored triple is the rotation `(0 1 2)` in each component. Its curve has genus one and its
geometry is Euclidean, the orders `(3, 3, 3)` having reciprocals summing to one; these invariants
are read off the isomorphic cyclic triple `TauCeti.PermutationTriple.cyclicPowTriple 3 1`. The
passport row and the map row `3T1-3_3_3-a` are valid, and their stored labels agree with their
certified fields.

The map row `6T6-6_6_3.3-a` has degree six, two six-cycles over `0` and `1`, and two three-cycles
over `∞`, so its curve has genus two and its geometry is hyperbolic. Its triple here, and with it
the sheet numbering of the primitivization block `{0, 3}`, is a representative of the passport
`6T6-6_6_3.3` chosen in this file; it is not checked against the literal permutations and block
of the frozen record. The row is valid for the passport of this triple. Its monodromy action is
imprimitive: the involution `ι = r³`, for `r` the rotation of the six sheets, is an automorphism
of the triple, so the monodromy group permutes the pairs `{a, ι a}`, and the pair `{0, 3}` is a
block. Every component moves every pair,
so on the three pairs each component is a three-cycle, and the quotient is the cyclic cover of
degree three. Geometrically, the genus-two curve is a double cover of the elliptic curve of
`3T1-3_3_3-a`, the quotient by the automorphism `ι`. The block is maximal, the quotient having
prime degree, and the map row `3T1-3_3_3-a` certifies the stored primitivization of the passport
row `6T6-6_6_3.3`, through this block of the representative triple.

This file does not certify the group component `6T6` of the degree-six labels, which is read
through the transitive-group reference data `TauCeti.numTransitiveGroups`, nor the passport size
of `6T6-6_6_3.3`; accordingly the degree-six passport row is not shown to satisfy
`TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.PassportRecord.IsValidAt`, and its labels are not parsed.

The equations, the curve links, and the labels of related objects of both map rows are carrier
data that validity does not read (`TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.BelyiRecord.isValidFor_congr`);
they are left empty here rather than reproduced.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.isValidAt_cyclicThreePassportRecord` and
  `TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.isValidFor_cyclicThreeBelyiRecord`: the rows of `3T1-3_3_3`
  are valid.
* `TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.isValidFor_genusTwoBelyiRecord`: the map row `6T6-6_6_3.3-a`,
  with a representative triple of its passport, is valid for that passport, of genus two.
* `TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.automorphismGroup_toTriple_genusTwoStoredTriple`: the
  automorphism group of the triple of `6T6-6_6_3.3-a` is generated by `r³`.
* `TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.equivalent_blockQuotient_toTriple_genusTwoStoredTriple`: its
  quotient by the translates of `{0, 3}` is isomorphic to the triple of `3T1-3_3_3-a`.
* `TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.eq_or_eq_univ_of_isBlock_toTriple_genusTwoStoredTriple`: the
  block `{0, 3}` is maximal.
* `TauCeti.PermutationTriple.LMFDB.isPrimitivizationOf_genusTwoPassportRecord`: the map row
  `3T1-3_3_3-a` certifies the primitivization of the passport row `6T6-6_6_3.3`.

## References

* M. Musty, S. Schiavone, J. Sijsling, J. Voight, *A database of Belyi maps*.
* LMFDB, [Belyi maps](https://www.lmfdb.org/Belyi/).
-/

open Equiv MulAction
open scoped Pointwise

public section

namespace TauCeti
